FreeSDN FFmpeg stable source build

FFmpeg 9.0.2 is obtained from https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ and checked with the
upstream release signature and pinned SHA-256. Public verification fingerprint:
FCF986EA15E6E293A5644F10B4322F04D67658D8.

Only what FreeSDN gives FFmpeg is compiled: RTSP and RTSPS camera input, the
video (H.264, H.265, MJPEG, MPEG-4, MPEG-1/2, AV1 through libdav1d) and audio
(G.711, G.722, G.723.1, G.726, G.729, AMR, L16, L24, AAC, AC-3, MPEG audio,
Opus) codecs cameras send, and the MJPEG, libx264,
AAC, MP4, HLS, scale and drawtext outputs. Every other decoder, encoder,
demuxer, muxer, filter, bitstream filter, hardware accelerator and device is
disabled, and build.sh checks the enabled component sets after configure. The
RTSP, MJPEG and WAV muxers and the Opus and PCM encoders serve go2rtc's own
FFmpeg transcodes.
ffplay is not built. The musl V4L2 ioctl compatibility patch from Alpine aports
community/ffmpeg (author q66, original commit
6408745f54ada32bad44227e6b4173e46641afaa) is still applied so the source matches
earlier builds, though no V4L2 device is compiled.

The build enables GPL and version3 options for x264 and OpenSSL. FFmpeg license
texts accompany the runtime. The exact upstream source archive, patch, recipe,
source lock, signature and public verification key are included under
/usr/share/freesdn-sources/ffmpeg. Build package versions and runtime binary
hashes are recorded there as well. Dependencies remain signed stable-Alpine
packages and require their own updates and license compliance. This source
bundle does not assert a complete legal review of every image dependency.

No Alpine edge repository, downloaded opaque runtime binary, setuid capability,
or private publisher signing key is required by this recipe.
